---js
const numberOfLatestPostsToShow = 5;
---

<p>I used to be the guy who fixed computers and installed cool things on your phone. Now I roll out ideas to the internet through high-quality and scalable websites.</p>

<p>
  I also craft frontend pieces at
  <a href="https://zeroeight.com.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zero Eight</a>
  and
  <a href="https://idgadvertising.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IDG Advertising</a>.
  You can follow what I'm up to lately on my <a href="/now">now page</a>.
</p>


{% set postsCount = collections.posts | length %}
{% set latestPostsCount = postsCount | min(numberOfLatestPostsToShow) %}
<h1>Latest {{ latestPostsCount }} post{% if latestPostsCount != 1 %}s{% endif %}</h1>

{% set postslist = collections.posts | head(-1 * numberOfLatestPostsToShow) %}
{% set postslistCounter = postsCount %}
{% include "postslist.njk" %}

{% set morePosts = postsCount - numberOfLatestPostsToShow %}
{% if morePosts > 0 %}
<p>{{ morePosts }} more post{% if morePosts != 1 %}s{% endif %} can be found in <a href="blog.njk">the archive</a>.</p>
{% endif %}

